WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.980
H-Hey, Hugo! If you go too fast, the Duel 
Chasers will pursue us again!

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.990
Yuzu, they're not gonna arrest us.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.490
We're official Friendship Cup participants.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.490
Just because I'm gunning it a little—

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.700
Oh, no... It's already started!

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.040
We've sighted the two in question.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.360
Shall we secure them before 
they enter the arena?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.960
I am not so heartless.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.350
Let us at least allow them to enjoy 
the opening ceremonies.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.870
It's Jack Atlas's big duel, after all.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.600
D-Wheels.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.800
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.510
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.170
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:35.570
The Duel King, Jack Atlas

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:40.830
Eagerly awaiting the Friendship Cup's start,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:44.110
over 200,000 spectators have packed into

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.250
the Duel Palace, which towers over City's center!

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:56.240
I'm Melissa Claire, and I am here with you, 
to enjoy the opening ceremony

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:01.390
of City's greatest duel tournament, 
the Friendship Cup!

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:11.300
To be chosen for such an important 
role... I sure am popular!

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.580
Where could the others have been taken?

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.130
Every year, during the Friendship Cup's 
opening ceremonies,

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.430
the reigning king holds an exhibition match.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:35.520
Why not let him be the opponent?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.540
Me?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.330
H-Hey! Where are you taking them?

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.370
Do not worry. We have no 
intention of harming them.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.810
They are Friendship Cup participants.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.960
Even if they tried to break out 
of prison, they are heroes...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.950
...just as long as they keep winning.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.820
Right, chairman?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.280
Yes.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.820
They will be our very welcome guests.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.020
As long as they keep winning.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.110
Yuzu must be watching from somewhere nearby!

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.760
Win and put her mind at ease!

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.230
Show these Synchro Dimension 
guys what we can do!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.700
Crush that traitor, Jack Atlas!

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.070
Traitor?

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.790
Hey, what kind of person is Jack Atlas?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.700
Um...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.360
Oh, were you told not to talk to me?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.660
No... Nothing like that.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.980
Are you a fan of Jack's?

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.930
Wh-Why do you ask?

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.470
I've heard that Jack is king to 
both Tops and Commons,

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.400
so I'm sure he has a lot of fans.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.640
I was wondering if you were one.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:05:00.080
Sorry... Since I'm fighting him, 
I guess it's hard to discuss.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.470
I was just wondering what kind of person he is.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.530
Um, three years ago,

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.890
Jack Atlas became the first Commons-born 
Friendship Cup winner.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.910
Ever since, he's reigned as king, 
the undisputed champion.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.540
The way he acts and speaks...

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:24.140
I think they're suited to the one said 
to be the greatest duelist ever...

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.610
Sorry, you seem uncomfortable 
talking about him.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.350
W-Well, it's just about time. 
I'll show you to the arena.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.720
Wait a minute, Hugo!

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.690
We're actually here! At the Duel Palace!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.660
It's so big! It's too huge!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.740
I really get to duel in a place like this?

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.630
My heart can't take it...

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.370
The Maiami City duel stadium was big,

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.840
but this riding-duel venue is even bigger!

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.270
Now, it's time to begin the main event.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:11.820
City's pride and joy, Duel King Jack Atlas, 
will now hold a special match!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:24.200
Jack! Jack! Jack! Jack! 
Jack! Jack! Jack! Jack!

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.900
Jack! Jack! Jack!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.130
Mr. Atlas!

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:33.610
That's what you get with Jack Atlas, 
symbol of the Friendship Cup!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:38.440
Tops and Commons come 
together to call his name!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.110
But wait just one minute...

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:46.800
I have to introduce the lucky duelist, 
chosen as the king's opponent

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.820
for this year's opening ceremony!

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.290
His name is

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.660
Yuya Sakaki!

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.270
Yuya?

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.570
Crow and the others told me about this,

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.870
but people really duel while riding these?

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:14.300
Is that Yuya?

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:19.420
What's wrong?

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.910
My bracelet...

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.990
Is it because you're both here?

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.120
Which means... That really must be...

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.250
Yuya!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.340
So that's Yuya?

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.080
I don't know why he was chosen to face Jack,

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.240
but I feel sorry for him.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.210
He's a sacrifice to the king.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.410
A sacrifice?

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:50.710
Do you know why they hold an exhibition 
match before the Friendship Cup starts?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.490
To show everyone the king's strength.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.680
The king doesn't fight in the tournament.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.000
He only fights the winner.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.300
In other words, the Friendship Cup is a 
contest for the right to duel the king.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:10.470
The exhibition match is to show 
how high he stands above everyone.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:16.280
So, every year, Jack crushes 
his opponent without mercy,

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.910
as if to tell competitors, "Climb up here and get me."

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.800
Well, it's a bit of a custom.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.550
Without mercy?

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.600
Yeah.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.030
That's why we call his exhibition 
opponent a "sacrifice."

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.990
That's awful.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.730
Now, the moment you've been 
waiting for... The king is here.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:41.450
City bows before his strength and majesty!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:45.900
Despite his Commons birth, he's driven the road 
to success, like a proverbial rising dragon.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:51.160
The living legend who stands 
atop duelists everywhere...

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.580
Introducing our King of Duelists, Jack Atlas!

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.140
There is but one king! And that is I!

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:20.610
Mr. Atlas!

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:27.780
Jack! Jack! Jack! Jack!

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:31.020
Jack Atlas really is cool.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.690
I have a question for you!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.890
What turn should I beat this kid on?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.560
That's obvious! Finish him on the first turn!

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.230
The king's duels must be entertaining!

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:49.930
Entertaining?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.140
Turn one...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:56.340
I'll take the first move. And after the curtain rises...

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.040
Turn two.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:00.750
I'll allow my opponent to show what he can do.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.450
Turn three.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:07.150
I'll finish with a display of the overwhelming 
difference in our skills!

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.790
Let us see what he has.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.960
Will the power of the Lancers...

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.360
...work against the Duel King?

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.410
It should be most interesting. Right, chairman?

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:22.180
Yes, let us watch very closely.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.700
Yuya...

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:35.540
Me, lose on turn three?

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.580
Crush that traitor, Jack Atlas!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.450
I'll show him how I entertain!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.840
First, I'll activate the Field Spell.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:50.930
Today, we'll change the rules up a bit 
by using an Action Field—

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.620
Wait, what?

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.000
An Action Field?

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.790
We granted your request.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:01.710
Duels that use the spell cards 
known as Action Cards...

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:06.040
That was the way you Lancers fought.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.360
Yes, in the battle against Academia.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:11.180
Modeling it after a real fight?

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.470
It should be something to see.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.890
Right, chairman?

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.270
Yes!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:23.480
I don't really get it. But Action Field, on.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.260
Crossover Acceleration!

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.510
Duel mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:43.690
Riding duel... Acceleration!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:45.430
Duel!

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.360
Autopilot, huh?

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.720
I see. Then, I can use my hands to duel.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:54.460
The first move is mine!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:12:00.700
Wow! Jack took the first turn, 
just as he said he would!

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.490
My turn!

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.670
I summon Red Sprinter from my hand.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:12.330
When this is the only monster on the field,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:16.950
I can Special Summon one Tuner Monster, 
Level 3 or below, from my hand.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.820
I Special Summon Red Resonator.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:28.990
Level 2 Red Resonator tunes Level 4 Red Sprinter!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.610
Let the scarlet souls become one.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.970
Tremble before the champion's war cry!

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:39.440
Synchro Summon!

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.750
Come out, Red Wyvern!

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.400
The king went right to a Synchro Summon!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.420
A truly stunning opening to the match!

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:56.300
Will the rest proceed as the king predicted?

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.340
Jack really is cool!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:00.890
He's the best!

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:03.760
I hope I can duel Jack soon, too!

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.960
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.290
Now, it's your turn.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.850
I'm giving you a chance to show your stuff.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.030
Don't disappoint me!

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.950
I'll show you my entertainment duel!

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.440
My turn!

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.950
I set the Pendulum Scale

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.300
with Scale 1 Stargazer Magician and 
Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:42.770
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.740
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.330
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:50.340
Pendulum Summon!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.240
Come out, my monsters!

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:58.940
First, Performapal Trump Girl.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.150
Next...

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.890
Performapal Teeter Totter Hopper.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:06.090
And Performapal Stamp Turtle.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.590
And now, the leading actor appears!

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.930
The rare dragon with two eyes of different colors,

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.070
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:17.400
Incredible... He's summoned four at once?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.600
In an earlier scoop, I, Melissa Claire, 
saw them summoning

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.740
two at once in Central Park, 
but this is twice that!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.480
Pendulum Summon is just too incredible!

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:30.440
Wow!

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:31.840
Impossible!

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:34.950
Yuya... That must really be Yuya!

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:40.260
With Performapal Trump Girl, I can use Pendulum 
Summoned monsters to Fusion Summon.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:45.660
I fuse Trump Girl and Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.380
The one who controls mysterious power,

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.220
transform into dazzling light and 
reside in the dragon's eye!

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.110
Fusion Summon!

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.560
Come out, the sky dragon that 
wields the secret arts.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.580
Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:12.420
And I overlay Level 4 Stamp Turtle 
and Skeeter Skimmer!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.460
From the black darkness,

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:23.990
the fangs of rebellion that fight against 
the powers of stupidity descend!

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.070
Xyz Summon!

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.700
Rank 4 Dark Rebellion Xyz Dragon!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.630
Is that his...

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.220
Yeah, Ute's dragon.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.520
Fusion and Xyz...

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:43.190
He uses a variety of summons?

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:46.510
Is this the power of the Lancers?

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:49.660
Not bad at all. Right, chairman?

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.900
Yes, this is quite impressive.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:16:01.670
Yuya Sakaki moves from the shocking 
Pendulum Summon to the unusual

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.610
Xyz and Fusion Summons, producing two dragons.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:10.550
But our hero Jack surely won't stand idly by.

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:12.540
Once, during your turn,

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:17.020
when you have two or more monsters with 
higher attack points than Red Wyvern's,

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:21.730
it can destroy the one with more attack points.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.930
I destroy Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.740
I won't let you!

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:33.120
Yes!

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.480
I activate Action Spell Mirror Barrier!

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.940
Its effect negates one monster's destruction.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.410
He blocked it!

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:46.120
Action Cards can do that? Amazing.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.660
No way.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.660
Using a card you just picked up...

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:50.590
Isn't that cheating?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.790
What a terribly interesting strategy.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.060
Indeed.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:58.760
I guess riding duels have evolved even further.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:00.260
Cool!

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.810
I can't lose on the third turn.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.700
This turn, I'll finish you!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:12.580
Dark Rebellion Xyz Dragon can use one 
of its Overlay Units to activate its effect.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.080
I use two Overlay Units!

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:19.140
I halve one of your monster's attack points,

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:22.750
to increase those of Dark Rebellion 
by the same amount.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.070
Treason Discharge!

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.780
I again use its effect to further 
halve those attack points.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:35.360
Now, the attack points of the 
challenger dragon are 4300!

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:38.100
This is trouble! It's big trouble!

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:42.310
Battle!

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:46.510
Go, Dark Rebellion! Attack Red Wyvern!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.930
Lightning Disobey of Rebellion!

00:17:56.120 --> 00:18:01.190
3700 damage at once! That's huge!

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.710
And the finish...

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:07.230
Go, Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.930
Attack Jack Atlas directly!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.170
No way! Will Jack Atlas lose? King!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:15.410
Mr. Atlas!

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:20.450
Continuous Shiny Burst!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:42.160
I activated my Action Spell Evasive Evasion,

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.470
to Special Summon an Evasive Evasion Token.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:48.720
Once per turn, an Evasive Evasion 
Token lets me negate one attack.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:53.080
I used this to negate Rune-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon's attack!

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.990
Great job!

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:57.050
Mr. Atlas is so smart!

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:59.920
He's already learned how to use Action Cards!

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:04.800
But Rune-Eyes attacks depending 
on the level of monsters

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.920
used as components in its fusion.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.400
Trump Girl's Level 2 lets it attack twice.

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:12.400
Therefore, it can attack once more!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.630
I attack Evasive Evasion Token!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.500
I activate my trap Reject Reborn!

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:22.260
I negate one of your monster's attacks, 
and end the Battle Phase!

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.490
Then, I destroy all monsters 
on my side of the field,

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:34.810
to Special Summon, from the 
graveyard, as many monsters

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.410
as I negated attacks from.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:37.320
What?

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:40.060
I negated two attacks!

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:45.330
Be reborn, Red Wyvern! Red Resonator!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.850
When Red Resonator is Special Summoned,

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:54.270
I recover life equal to the attack points 
of one Synchro Monster on the field.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:58.780
I recover 2400 life points, equal to 
Red Wyvern's attack points!

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.560
Incredible! Not only did he evade the attack,

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:07.020
he returned two of his monsters to the 
field, even recovering some life!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.750
That's the Jack we know!

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.410
Our Jack!

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:13.260
The champion of champions, king of kings!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.360
I end my turn...

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.940
In that instant, Dark Rebellion's 
attack points return to normal.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:33.050
Great one, Jack! You rock!

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.380
Yuya...

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:37.700
You mentioned having an entertainment 
duel, didn't you?

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:42.290
But your way of dueling is mere self-satisfaction.

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.460
It is a far cry from entertainment!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.660
You lack the power to climb to 
the summit where I stand!

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.690
My turn!

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:03.910
Level 2 Red Resonator tunes 
Level 6 Red Wyvern!

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:11.580
The cry of the champion shakes 
heaven and earth.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.550
Let the conqueror's unique power 
be carved into your body!

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.020
Synchro Summon!

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.450
The raging soul...

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:23.350
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:28.120
Once per turn, Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:32.740
can destroy all Special Summoned monsters 
with lower attack points than its own.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:37.600
And for each, it deals 500 
points of damage to you.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.710
Absolute Power Flame!

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:52.760
Then, I attack directly with 
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:56.730
Red Hot Crimson Hell Burning!

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:58.960
Kneel before your king!

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.140
Yuya!

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.580
The special match of the Friendship 
Cup's opening ceremonies.

00:23:55.580 --> 00:24:02.080
And naturally, the winner was our 
King of Duelists, Jack Atlas!

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.800
Your duels are mere self-satisfaction.

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:07.320
They are a far cry from entertainment!

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:11.910
My father taught me this way of dueling. 
I won't let you mock it, Jack!

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:16.730
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Shattered Entertainment.

00:24:17.170 --> 00:24:19.290
The fun is only getting started!
